<h2>Keep safety in the decision</h2>
<p>Use the official <a href="https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/ashwagandha">NCCIH ashwagandha</a>, <a href="https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/rhodiola">NCCIH rhodiola</a> and <a href="https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Magnesium-Consumer/">NIH magnesium</a> summaries to prepare questions for a clinician or pharmacist. Bring the exact label and your medicine list. Do not assume that combining products is safe because each is sold separately.</p>
<p>Our earlier supplement ranking, general dosing stack and promised response timelines have been removed. They were not justified as recommendations for individual readers.</p>
<h2>Can Cortisol+ test whether a supplement worked?</h2>
<p>No. The app does not measure cortisol and has no validated supplement-response test. A change in HRV, sleep or the wellness score cannot isolate a product effect. The <a href="/how-it-works/">methodology</a> explains what the score uses. Clinical testing and treatment decisions need their own rationale.</p>
